  The design is not a classical DID design, a staggered adoption
  design, or an heterogeneous adoption design. On the other hand, it
  is a staggered first switch design: some groups experience their
  first treatment switch at different dates.

  First switches occur between t=2008 and t=2009.

  Estimator: did_multiplegt_dyn, with the continuous() option

  As the period-one treatment is continuously distributed (all groups
  have different period-one treatment), the did_multiplegt_dyn package
  needs to be used with the continuous option.

  See Chapter 8 of the DID textbook. In particular, see section
  8.3.5.1 for details on the continuous option.
